 ### [Training Loss Computation with Huber and Masking](4765-training-loss-computation-with-huber-and-masking.md)
-[Training Loss Computation with Huber and Masking](4765-training-loss-computation-with-huber-and-masking.md) defines the training-time pipeline using Huber loss ($\delta=0.1$) and binary ray validity masks. It differs from Masked Volume Metrics by operating on rays during training rather than froxels during evaluation, and from this family's general definition by specifying the Huber function and JAX-based implementation details.
